{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41718128",
      "title": "Styling NextJS Project: Your Options & Using CSS Modules",
      "sourceHash": "212f5a9c470c1721d6c5ef03fc9bd2e632c42a804516a3a6d39c7078d91452ea",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 3.75,
          "en": "So let's work on styling this header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.75,
          "end": 7.89,
          "en": "And when it comes to styling NextJS projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.89,
          "end": 10.35,
          "en": "you got a couple of different options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.35,
          "end": 13.503,
          "en": "as is the case for React projects as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.4,
          "end": 18.09,
          "en": "Now you can already see one option in this project here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.09,
          "end": 22.83,
          "en": "and that is such a global CSS file as I have it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.83,
          "end": 25.74,
          "en": "And you could add multiple global CSS files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.74,
          "end": 27.09,
          "en": "The names are up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.09,
          "end": 30.27,
          "en": "They are global because they're getting imported like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.27,
          "end": 34.68,
          "en": "in the layout JSS file in the RootLayout JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.68,
          "end": 38.52,
          "en": "And therefore any CSS file that's being imported like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.52,
          "end": 40.98,
          "en": "into this RootLayout JSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.98,
          "end": 43.32,
          "en": "will be available on every page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.32,
          "end": 47.31,
          "en": "And the styles set up here will be available on every page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.31,
          "end": 48.603,
          "en": "That's the great thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.53,
          "end": 54.21,
          "en": "But this is not the only way of styling NextJS projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.21,
          "end": 58.29,
          "en": "Another popular option for styling NextJS projects is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.29,
          "end": 60.039,
          "en": "to use Tailwind CSS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.039,
          "end": 64.32,
          "en": "because Tailwind in general is pretty popular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.32,
          "end": 67.71,
          "en": "It's a CSS library that allows you to style elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.71,
          "end": 71.78999999999999,
          "en": "by adding small utility classes to those elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.78999999999999,
          "end": 74.52,
          "en": "And indeed, on the Tailwind website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.52,
          "end": 78.69,
          "en": "you also find instructions on how you could add Tailwind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.69,
          "end": 81,
          "en": "to a NextJS project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81,
          "end": 84.51,
          "en": "And in addition, when creating a new NextJS project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.51,
          "end": 89.1,
          "en": "you are also asked whether you want to add Tailwind CSS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.1,
          "end": 92.34,
          "en": "at least at the point of time where I recorded this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.34,
          "end": 95.64,
          "en": "So getting started with Tailwind in Next project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.64,
          "end": 98.34,
          "en": "is pretty easy and Tailwind as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.34,
          "end": 102.57300000000001,
          "en": "indeed is also a popular solution for styling those apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.56,
          "end": 106.97999999999999,
          "en": "But we're not going to use it in this project, simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.97999999999999,
          "end": 109.65,
          "en": "because I don't wanna bore you by adding a bunch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.65,
          "end": 113.03999999999999,
          "en": "of CSS classes to my JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.03999999999999,
          "end": 117.24000000000001,
          "en": "And that is what we would have to do when using Tailwind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 117.24000000000001,
          "end": 120.51,
          "en": "So it's amazing but not great for a course like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.51,
          "end": 124.47,
          "en": "where I want to focus on the main topic, which is NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.47,
          "end": 129.15,
          "en": "and React, not Tailwind, therefore I'll not use it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.15,
          "end": 130.8,
          "en": "but you could use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.8,
          "end": 134.97,
          "en": "Instead, here in this section we'll use another solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 134.97,
          "end": 137.4,
          "en": "that's supported by NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.4,
          "end": 140.76,
          "en": "and that would be CSS modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.76,
          "end": 144.66,
          "en": "which is in general standard CSS code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.66,
          "end": 148.41,
          "en": "but scoped to specific components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.41,
          "end": 152.7,
          "en": "by assigning special names to your CSS files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.7,
          "end": 156.21,
          "en": "And that's supported by NextJS out of the box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 156.21,
          "end": 160.29,
          "en": "And the idea simply is that you add CSS files that end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.29,
          "end": 163.14,
          "en": "with dot module dot css",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 163.14,
          "end": 167.16,
          "en": "and you can then import an object from those files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 167.16,
          "end": 169.14,
          "en": "which will be generated automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.14,
          "end": 171.06,
          "en": "by the underlying build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 171.06,
          "end": 174.36,
          "en": "and development server, which gives you access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.36,
          "end": 179.36,
          "en": "to all the CSS classes defined in those files as properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.81,
          "end": 182.34,
          "en": "And that's what I'll do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 182.34,
          "end": 184.89,
          "en": "And therefore I prepared a CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 184.89,
          "end": 189.89,
          "en": "for you, a main header CSS file, which you can add next",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 190.29,
          "end": 192.513,
          "en": "to that main header JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 194.161,
          "end": 196.74,
          "en": "And in that main header CSS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 196.74,
          "end": 201.51,
          "en": "I'm simply setting up a bunch of CSS classes and styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 201.51,
          "end": 204.09,
          "en": "You can of course tweak them as you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 204.09,
          "end": 206.133,
          "en": "but it should also work like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 207.03,
          "end": 209.315,
          "en": "Now we just have to import them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 209.315,
          "end": 213.623,
          "en": "or import this file into this main header JSS file to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 213.623,
          "end": 218.623,
          "en": "activate it and to make those classes available in this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 218.7,
          "end": 221.643,
          "en": "and scope those classes to this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 222.75,
          "end": 225.999,
          "en": "And for that, we need a special way of importing this, not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 225.999,
          "end": 230.4,
          "en": "as we imported CSS in the layout JSS file like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 230.4,
          "end": 234.72,
          "en": "That would simply add the CSS classes as global classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 234.72,
          "end": 237.663,
          "en": "that affect all pages and all components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 238.56,
          "end": 242.28,
          "en": "but instead by using import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 242.28,
          "end": 246.42,
          "en": "and then any name of your choice like classes from,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 247.68,
          "end": 250.98,
          "en": "and then main header module CSS, in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 250.98,
          "end": 253.263,
          "en": "a relative path to that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 255.51,
          "end": 260.16,
          "en": "And with that added, you can now use this classes object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 260.16,
          "end": 263.76,
          "en": "which it is to access certain properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 263.76,
          "end": 266.07,
          "en": "And every class defined here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 266.07,
          "end": 270.42,
          "en": "in this main header module CSS file will simply be available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 270.42,
          "end": 273.093,
          "en": "as a property on this imported object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 274.40999999999997,
          "end": 277.56,
          "en": "So for example, here on this logo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 277.56,
          "end": 281.15999999999997,
          "en": "we can assign a class to this link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 281.15999999999997,
          "end": 285.78,
          "en": "And we now don't do this as a string like some class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 285.78,
          "end": 288.57,
          "en": "but instead as a dynamic value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 288.57,
          "end": 291.6,
          "en": "where we access this class's object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 291.6,
          "end": 294.183,
          "en": "And then here it's the logo class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 295.53,
          "end": 298.47,
          "en": "And this will apply this class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 298.47,
          "end": 302.16,
          "en": "and all the other related styles to this link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 302.16,
          "end": 304.35,
          "en": "and the nested elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 304.35,
          "end": 307.14,
          "en": "But it's doing that such that the styles are scoped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 307.14,
          "end": 310.83,
          "en": "to this component and can't affect any other component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 310.83,
          "end": 312.39,
          "en": "on the page, even if you would",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 312.39,
          "end": 314.343,
          "en": "use a similar class name there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 316.8,
          "end": 318.78,
          "en": "So that's the first step here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 318.78,
          "end": 321.18,
          "en": "In addition, I also want to add a class name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 321.18,
          "end": 325.92,
          "en": "to the header itself, and that would be classes.header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 325.92,
          "end": 329.73,
          "en": "And then on the navigation, I want to add a class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 329.73,
          "end": 334.293,
          "en": "to this nav element here with classes.nav.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 335.58,
          "end": 338.40999999999997,
          "en": "With all that done, if you save that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 339.33,
          "end": 341.1,
          "en": "and you go back to your page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 341.1,
          "end": 343.02,
          "en": "this now looks much better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 343.02,
          "end": 347.13,
          "en": "Now we got a properly styled header, a properly styled logo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 347.13,
          "end": 350.73,
          "en": "and these navigation links here, which also look better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 350.73,
          "end": 353.79,
          "en": "and which of course also still work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 353.79,
          "end": 356.88,
          "en": "But now all styled in a beautiful way with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 356.88,
          "end": 358.383,
          "en": "of CSS modules.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}